   "Knots in the Skyrme-Faddeev model",
   "Paul Sutcliffe"
  ],
  "abstract": "The Skyrme-Faddeev model is a modi\ufb01ed sigma model in three-d imensional space, which has string-like topological solitons classi\ufb01ed by th e integer-valued Hopf charge. Numerical simulations are performed to compute soliton sol utions for Hopf charges up to sixteen, with initial conditions provided by families of rational maps from the three- sphere into the complex projective line. A large number of ne w solutions are presented, including a variety of torus knots for a range of Hopf charges . Often these knots are only local energy minima, with the global minimum being a lin ked solution, but for some values of the Hopf charge they are good candidates for th e global minimum energy solution. The computed energies are in agreement wit h Ward\u2019s conjectured energy bound. 1",
